101,quintessence,noun,C1,most perfect example or embodiment,The painting captured the quintessence of elegance.,Quintessence defined the era's style,You recognized the essence,,"The chef's new dish captured the quintessence of traditional cuisine while using modern techniques. The perfect balance represented the very best of both approaches. The quintessence of flavor emerged from carefully selected ingredients. The dish became her signature, embodying the quintessence of her style. Diners praised the quintessence of culinary skill demonstrated.",LexaWall Educational Content,"The grandmother was the quintessence of grace, kindness, and wisdom. She embodied the best qualities of her generation. Her quintessence as a human being inspired everyone around her.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
102,recondite,adjective,C1,difficult to understand; little known,He studied recondite medieval manuscripts quietly.,Recondite theories challenged casual readers,You encountered obscure concepts,,The academic paper explored recondite aspects of ancient philosophy few scholars had seriously studied. The specialized knowledge required years of preparation to understand. References to recondite concepts made the work inaccessible to general readers. Experts appreciated the recondite scholarship even as its audience remained tiny. The recondite nature of the work elevated her standing in scholarly circles.,LexaWall Educational Content,The magician's recondite knowledge of sleight of hand fascinated enthusiasts. His mastery of obscure techniques set him apart from other performers. The recondite skill made his performances seem impossibly magical.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
103,relegate,verb,C1,assign to a lower position or status,They relegated the issue to a subcommittee.,Management relegated the topic to later,You assigned it lesser priority,,"The decision to relegate the issue to a subcommittee effectively sidelined it from important discussions. Important work got postponed as the committee structure delayed decisions. The attempt to relegate thorny problems didn't make them disappear. Eventually, relegate issues rebounded requiring attention. Key decisions had been delayed by relegating concerns.",LexaWall Educational Content,She refused to relegate her ambitious dreams to the background despite family pressure. Her determination not to be relegated to limited roles drove her success. Rejecting the expectation to relegate her ambitions paid off.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
104,remonstrate,verb,C1,protest or object strongly and earnestly,Stakeholders remonstrated against the proposed cuts.,Citizens remonstrated at the hearing,You voiced strong objections,,Community members decided to remonstrate against the proposed factory near residential areas. Their strong objections at the hearing influenced the decision-making process. The passionate remonstration from residents delayed approval. Officials heard clearly how residents would remonstrate if they ignored concerns. The remonstrate voice of the community proved decisive.,LexaWall Educational Content,"The referee began to remonstrate with the player about his excessive roughness. She objected forcefully to his playing style and warned about fouls. When he refused to remonstrate against the roughness, she ejected him.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
105,reprieve,noun,C1,temporary relief from harm or punishment,The court granted a reprieve for two weeks.,A reprieve postponed the final decision,You gained a temporary pause,,The death row inmate received a reprieve just hours before execution. The temporary stay allowed time for new evidence review. The reprieve eventually became permanent when innocence was proven. What began as temporary reprieve from execution became freedom. The reprieve changed his entire life.,LexaWall Educational Content,The reprieve from homework allowed her to recover from exhaustion. The temporary break gave space to rest and recharge. The reprieve came at exactly the right moment.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
106,rescind,verb,C1,revoke or cancel officially,The council rescinded the earlier ordinance.,They rescinded the flawed regulation,You nullified the order,,The university voted to rescind the controversial policy after student protests. The decision to rescind reflected reconsideration of the impacts. Rescind votes followed similar decisions at other institutions. The ability to rescind earlier choices showed institutional flexibility. Reversing course through rescind was rare but important.,LexaWall Educational Content,The company decided to rescind its contract with the problematic vendor. The rescind action followed quality control failures. Rescinding the agreement prevented further complications.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
107,reticent,adjective,C1,unwilling to speak openly,He remained reticent during the intense questioning.,Reticent witnesses withheld extra detail,You chose to stay silent,,The reticent witness offered minimal information despite aggressive questioning. His unwillingness to speak openly frustrated investigators. The reticent responses suggested he was hiding something. Even direct questions couldn't overcome his reticence. The witness remained reticent throughout the proceedings.,LexaWall Educational Content,"She was reticent about her accomplishments, deflecting praise uncomfortable. Her reticent nature reflected both humility and shyness. Encouraging her to speak openly about her reticent experiences helped.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
108,reverie,noun,C1,a state of being pleasantly lost in thought,Her reverie was broken by a sharp knock.,A sudden noise ended his reverie,You drifted into thought,,The musician's reverie at the piano lasted hours as she lost herself in composition. Her dreamy state produced some of her finest work. The reverie was interrupted only by necessity. Colleagues learned not to disturb her during reverie. These transcendent moments of reverie drove her creative genius.,LexaWall Educational Content,"His reverie about childhood memories was broken by the honking horn. For a moment, he'd been lost in pleasant thought. The sudden noise ended his peaceful reverie abruptly.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
109,sagacious,adjective,C1,having keen practical sense and wisdom,"The board sought sagacious, experienced counsel.",A sagacious mentor guided the team,You applied wise judgment,,The sagacious elder's advice drew from decades of experience and keen observation. His wise counsel helped younger people avoid mistakes. The sagacious perspective guided important decisions. Seeking his sagacious input became common practice. His sagacious wisdom benefited many who listened.,LexaWall Educational Content,Her sagacious analysis of market trends identified opportunities others missed. The wise insight gave her competitive advantage. Her sagacious understanding of her industry was remarkable.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
110,sanguine,adjective,B2,optimistic about a future outcome,They remained sanguine despite the setbacks.,Sanguine forecasts lifted investor spirits,You kept optimistic outlook,,"Despite setbacks, the team remained sanguine about their eventual success. Their optimistic outlook inspired continued effort even through failures. The sanguine perspective prevented despondency. Whether the sanguine attitude was realistic or naive remained debatable. The sanguine team persisted toward their goal.",LexaWall Educational Content,The coach's sanguine forecast predicted victory despite the opposing team's superior record. His optimistic belief in his players' ability motivated them. The sanguine prediction influenced team confidence positively.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
111,scintillating,adjective,C1,brilliantly lively and stimulating,She delivered a scintillating and witty lecture.,Scintillating remarks enlivened the debate,You felt intellectually stirred,,The lecturer delivered a scintillating presentation that captivated every audience member. Her brilliant wit and engaging style made complex ideas accessible. The scintillating performance earned enthusiastic applause. Students credited her scintillating delivery with inspiring their interest. The scintillating evening remained memorable.,LexaWall Educational Content,The scintillating conversation between the two intellectuals impressed everyone listening. Their witty repartee and brilliant observations delighted the small gathering. The scintillating exchange demonstrated intellectual excellence.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
112,serendipity,noun,C1,finding valuable things by chance,Their meeting was pure serendipity and timing.,A moment of serendipity changed careers,You appreciated the fortunate chance,,Their collaboration began through serendipity when both were stranded at an airport. The chance meeting led to a creative partnership exceeding both expectations. The serendipity of being in the same place at the right moment changed their careers. Neither could have planned the serendipity that brought them together. They remained grateful for the fortunate chance.,LexaWall Educational Content,Finding the vintage record at the flea market felt like pure serendipity. She'd been looking for years without success. The serendipity of discovery made the find even more precious.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
113,solicitous,adjective,C1,showing care or concern for others,He was solicitous about her recovery.,Solicitous colleagues checked on her often,You noticed their concern,,"The solicitous friend checked on her recovery daily, bringing food and offering help. Her caring concern touched the patient deeply. The solicitous attention accelerated the healing process emotionally. The solicitous support made isolation less difficult. Gratitude for her solicitous care remained lasting.",LexaWall Educational Content,The solicitous waiter anticipated needs before customers articulated them. His careful attention to detail impressed diners. The solicitous service enhanced the dining experience.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
114,specious,adjective,C1,seemingly plausible but actually wrong,The argument's logic proved specious on inspection.,Specious reasoning misled several readers,You saw the flaw,,The argument's logic sounded initially convincing but proved specious upon closer examination. The seemingly valid reasoning masked significant flaws. The specious appeal to emotion substituted for actual evidence. Careful analysis revealed the specious nature of the claim. The specious reasoning ultimately persuaded no informed observers.,LexaWall Educational Content,"His explanation seemed plausible but was actually specious, relying on false assumptions. The specious logic masked dishonesty. Eventually, she realized the specious nature of his account.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
115,stoic,adjective,C1,enduring pain without complaint,She remained stoic during difficult negotiations.,His stoic demeanor calmed the room,You withstood the pressure,,"The stoic athlete endured the pain without complaint, focusing on completing the race. Her refusal to surrender to discomfort impressed observers. The stoic determination overcame physical limitations. Her stoic composure inspired teammates facing their own struggles. The stoic attitude became her trademark.",LexaWall Educational Content,He maintained stoic calm as bad news kept arriving. His composed response prevented panic. His stoic demeanor showed remarkable inner strength.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
116,superfluous,adjective,C1,exceeding what is necessary,Redundant clauses made the draft superfluous.,Superfluous details cluttered the proposal,You trimmed the excess,,The lengthy introduction contained superfluous information that could have been removed. The excess detail distracted from the main message. Cutting superfluous passages improved the presentation significantly. The editor identified superfluous sections that weakened the argument. Trimming the superfluous strengthened the final product.,LexaWall Educational Content,The decorative details were beautiful but seemed superfluous to the building's function. The architect later regretted adding unnecessary elements. The superfluous ornament complicated future renovations.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
117,surreptitious,adjective,C1,kept secret because illicit,They exchanged surreptitious notes in class.,A surreptitious glance sealed the deal,You noticed the covert act,,The surreptitious glance between the conspirators revealed their secret understanding. No one else noticed their covert communication. The surreptitious exchange happened almost invisibly. Their surreptitious coordination worked perfectly. No one suspected the surreptitious plot.,LexaWall Educational Content,He took a surreptitious photo of the document for later reference. The covert action violated policies but provided needed information. The surreptitious snapshot enabled him to solve the mystery.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
118,sycophant,noun,C1,one who flatters for personal gain,The committee tolerated a minor sycophant among them.,A sycophant praised every decision,You detected the flattery,,The executive surrounded himself with sycophants who praised every decision uncritically. His yes-men prevented honest feedback that might have improved outcomes. The sycophants' flattery isolated him from reality. Employees who weren't sycophants eventually left. The sycophantic environment prevented necessary course corrections.,LexaWall Educational Content,She recognized him as a sycophant using flattery for personal gain. His insincerity was transparent to those paying attention. She rejected his sycophantic attention firmly.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
119,taciturn,adjective,C1,reserved in speech; saying little,The new director proved taciturn in meetings.,Taciturn responses limited the discussion,You waited for fuller answers,,"The taciturn CEO spoke rarely in meetings, but everyone listened intently when he did. His limited words carried significant weight. The taciturn communication style meant every statement mattered. Employees respected that he didn't waste time on unnecessary talking. His taciturn nature contrasted sharply with his verbose predecessor.",LexaWall Educational Content,Her taciturn response suggested she preferred not to discuss the topic. The brief answer discouraged further questions. His taciturn nature made him difficult to understand.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
120,tantamount,adjective,C1,equivalent in effect or value,Refusal is tantamount to conceding defeat.,His silence was tantamount to agreement,You treated it as acceptance,,His refusal to take a stand was tantamount to supporting the status quo. Silence on injustice amounted to complicity. She understood his inaction was tantamount to endorsement. The refusal was tantamount to a clear answer. His silence proved tantamount to betrayal.,LexaWall Educational Content,The rejection was tantamount to saying her work wasn't valuable. The harsh dismissal stung more than a gentle refusal. His action was tantamount to public humiliation.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
121,temerity,noun,C1,rash boldness; foolish daring,No one expected such temerity from the novice.,Her temerity surprised the conservative board,You felt shocked by boldness,,The junior employee had the temerity to challenge the senior vice president's decision. Her bold questioning surprised everyone expecting silence. The temerity of the challenge impressed some while angering others. She paid a price for her temerity in the form of reduced opportunities. Yet her courageous temerity eventually led to promotion.,LexaWall Educational Content,He had the temerity to ask for a raise despite poor performance. His audacious request seemed foolish to everyone. The temerity of asking when results didn't support it cost him credibility.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
122,tenuous,adjective,C1,very weak or slight in substance,The evidence was tenuous at best.,Tenuous links undermined the hypothesis,You doubted its strength,,The evidence linking him to the crime was tenuous at best. The weak connection didn't convince skeptical observers. The tenuous case relied on circumstantial details. Building a prosecution on such tenuous ground seemed risky. The tenuous nature of the evidence made conviction unlikely.,LexaWall Educational Content,"Their relationship had become tenuous after repeated arguments. The weak connection barely held together. Saving the tenuous relationship required serious effort. Without intervention, the tenuous bonds would snap.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
123,terse,adjective,C1,brief and abruptly concise,His terse directive left room for interpretation.,A terse memo created further questions,You got the short message,,The terse directive from leadership left no room for interpretation or discussion. Her brief statement conveyed necessary information efficiently. The terse communication style prevented rambling or confusion. Some appreciated the terse efficiency while others found it cold. The terse approach reflected her preference for action over words.,LexaWall Educational Content,His terse reply suggested irritation with her question. The brief response ended the conversation immediately. Her terse manner made further conversation uncomfortable.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
124,torpor,noun,C1,state of physical or mental inactivity,After lunch she succumbed to pleasant torpor.,A weekend of torpor followed exams,You experienced sluggish rest,,The afternoon heat induced a pleasant torpor that made everyone want to nap. The sluggish inertia affected productivity throughout the company. Working against the torpor felt pointless to tired employees. Breaking through the torpor required significant effort. The torpor lifted only when evening brought cooler temperatures.,LexaWall Educational Content,"After the marathon, she sank into torpor, unable to move or think. The physical exhaustion created mental sluggishness. Recovering from her torpor took days.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
125,tortuous,adjective,C1,full of twists and turns; complex,The argument followed a tortuous series of claims.,Tortuous reasoning confused many readers,You lost track of logic,,The tortuous logic of his argument twisted back on itself repeatedly. Following his reasoning required intense concentration. The tortuous path through the argument made his conclusion unconvincing. Simpler reasoning might have been more persuasive. The tortuous nature of his logic undermined his case.,LexaWall Educational Content,The tortuous mountain road wound back and forth endlessly. The twisting path took hours to traverse despite short distance. The tortuous route prevented traveling at normal speeds.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
126,tractable,adjective,C1,easily managed or controlled,The volunteers proved surprisingly tractable and helpful.,A tractable schedule eased coordination,You adjusted plans smoothly,,"The new employee proved remarkably tractable and eager to learn. Her willingness to adjust and accept guidance impressed management. The tractable attitude made training her easy and pleasant. Unlike difficult personalities, her tractable nature facilitated teamwork. Her tractable approach to feedback accelerated her development.",LexaWall Educational Content,The dog's tractable nature made training simple and enjoyable. Her willingness to respond to commands exceeded expectations. The tractable behavior reflected her good temperament.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
127,transient,adjective,C1,lasting only a short time,Transient visitors populated the coastal town.,Transient moods altered daily attendance,You expected temporary change,,"The transient population of the tourist destination shifted seasonally. Visitors came and went, preventing community cohesion. The transient nature of the population complicates service planning. Local merchants adapted to transient customers with seasonal strategies. The transient crowds meant constant change.",LexaWall Educational Content,Her transient interest in hobbies meant she quickly moved to new pursuits. What fascinated her yesterday bored her today. The transient nature of her enthusiasms frustrated her family.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
128,trepidation,noun,C1,fear or agitation about future uncertainty,She approached the interview with trepidation.,Trepidation lingered before the verdict,You felt uneasy anticipation,,"She approached her first day of work with trepidation, nervous about making mistakes. Her anxiety about the new environment was understandable. The trepidation slowly faded as she became comfortable. By week's end, her initial trepidation had vanished. The trepidation turned into confidence.",LexaWall Educational Content,He listened to the verdict with mounting trepidation about the outcome. The fear of disappointing consequences overwhelmed him. His trepidation proved justified when the verdict came down.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
129,truculent,adjective,C1,eager to argue or fight aggressively,His truculent response escalated the debate quickly.,Truculent comments disrupted constructive dialogue,You faced hostile retorts,,"The truculent player's aggressive attitude toward referees got him ejected frequently. His eager combativeness alienated teammates and officials alike. The truculent demeanor on the field extended to locker room interactions. His truculent nature made him difficult to manage. Eventually, his truculence cost him his position.",LexaWall Educational Content,"The truculent response to criticism escalated tensions immediately. Rather than discussion, her hostile approach prevented dialogue. The truculent attitude made conflict resolution impossible.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
130,ubiquitous,adjective,B2,present or found everywhere,Smartphones are ubiquitous in urban settings.,Ubiquitous logos appeared across campus,You noticed their everywhere presence,,"Smartphones have become ubiquitous, appearing in virtually every pocket and purse. The near-universal presence changed how people communicate. The ubiquitous technology is now assumed rather than noteworthy. Finding someone without a ubiquitous smartphone has become unusual. The ubiquitous devices shaped modern behavior.",LexaWall Educational Content,"The ubiquitous logo appeared on clothing, bags, and advertisements everywhere. The brand's omnipresent marketing made the ubiquitous symbol familiar. The ubiquitous presence dominated visual culture.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
131,ulterior,adjective,C1,kept hidden; intentionally concealed motive,They suspected an ulterior motive behind donations.,Ulterior motives complicated the negotiations,You suspected hidden aims,,She suspected an ulterior motive behind his sudden kindness and offers to help. The hidden agenda she sensed made her wary. His ulterior motives eventually became clear when he asked for money. Accepting help meant risking entanglement with his ulterior intentions. The ulterior agenda complicated their relationship.,LexaWall Educational Content,The company's public commitment to the cause masked ulterior motives about profits. Their stated values hid different priorities. The ulterior agenda drove their actual decisions.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
132,umbrage,noun,C1,offense or annoyance at perceived insult,She took umbrage at the casual remark.,A slight caused visible umbrage in committee,You took personal offense,,"She took umbrage at the casual remark, interpreting it as insulting. The perceived slight hurt her feelings deeply. His dismissal of her umbrage as overreacting made it worse. She felt umbrage at both the original comment and his response. The umbrage festered for weeks.",LexaWall Educational Content,The umbrage between the neighbors escalated from minor disagreements to serious conflict. Each took offense at perceived slights. The accumulated umbrage created lasting hostility.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
133,unctuous,adjective,C1,excessively flattering in a smooth way,His unctuous praise felt manipulatively polite.,An unctuous handshake betrayed intent,You doubted the sincerity,,The unctuous salesman's excessive flattery made the customer uncomfortable. His oily manner of speaking felt manipulative and false. The unctuous charm was transparently insincere. She recognized his unctuous behavior as professional manipulation. His unctuous approach actually prevented her from trusting him.,LexaWall Educational Content,The unctuous praise in the recommendation letter rang false to objective readers. Its effusive language suggested exaggeration rather than truth. The unctuous tone undermined the letter's credibility.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
134,untenable,adjective,C1,not able to be defended or justified,That position became politically untenable quickly.,Untenable claims collapsed under scrutiny,You withdrew support,,"The company's position became politically untenable when evidence contradicted their claims. The unsustainable stance could no longer be defended credibly. Leadership recognized the untenable situation required reversal. The untenable policy faced intense opposition. Eventually, they abandoned the untenable position.",LexaWall Educational Content,The untenable theory collapsed under scrutiny from multiple research teams. The indefensible claim couldn't survive close examination. The untenable hypothesis was abandoned.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
135,vacillate,verb,C1,alternate between opinions or actions,He continued to vacillate over the project scope.,Investors vacillated before final commitment,You wavered on the choice,,"The indecisive leader continued to vacillate between options rather than choosing. His alternating between positions frustrated employees needing clear direction. The vacillation prevented decisive action. Teams grew tired of the vacillate leadership style. Finally, someone else made the decision the vacillating leader couldn't.",LexaWall Educational Content,"She continued to vacillate between accepting and declining the job offer. The competing desires made decision impossible. After weeks of vacillation, she finally chose.",LexaWall Educational Content,1
136,vacuous,adjective,C1,lacking intelligence or ideas; empty,The speech sounded vapid and vacuous throughout.,Vacuous slogans offered no real solution,You found it empty-headed,,"The speech seemed vapid and vacuous, containing no substantive ideas. The empty rhetoric said nothing meaningful despite many words. Listeners grew frustrated with the vacuous content. The vacuous nature of the message disappointed those seeking actual information. The vacuous address changed no minds.",LexaWall Educational Content,His vacuous response to the serious question showed he hadn't been listening. The empty-headed answer suggested lack of intelligence. The vacuous nature of his reply was insulting.,LexaWall Educational Content,1
